my-id "q-8715" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $0$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=\\pi +{x}_{1}=\\pi +0=\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=0,\\pi .$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=0\\cdot \\pi =0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8715/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8715"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-20414"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040762/assets/f00d8bd6cbd1f113df7f023e161e4d79e2f4a81157d1ac9a8ab65e70b4959221.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$  Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $B.$" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n$$\n\n Now, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies inside $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi $ hence, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ This is the $x$ coordinate of $A.$\n\nTo get another solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +x=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $B$ is $\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-72829/selection/1a4ee89f0618612cc5673272ad35e8d4625ee9ed24d34bd6027e2e3a826aae92" :answer/id #uuid "fccff7b1-4756-5608-8f85-48242f7d6791" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72829/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer/id #uuid "b3f9d6e7-dc7d-5361-a47a-0f41e590fc34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72829/selection/fc4e157478869e2cc16df8ee4cd323015b95523464d3b9a082af315c2a4fb28d" :answer/id #uuid "c535e997-0a1b-5a3b-9de6-388f4be826fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72829/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" :answer/id #uuid "06e44d1c-5727-574f-9456-55f484edbf7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72829/selection/35d0af53e25a7911f6d08c6d063fcf9231a1273a16a0f7056530d6f5d5dfbdd8" :answer/id #uuid "753265bd-6bc0-55f9-b310-90be13f48324" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72829/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "337be623-0765-5208-8fa1-c7a6844e7598" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72829/selection/35d0af53e25a7911f6d08c6d063fcf9231a1273a16a0f7056530d6f5d5dfbdd8" :answer-field/choices ["q-72829/selection/1a4ee89f0618612cc5673272ad35e8d4625ee9ed24d34bd6027e2e3a826aae92" "q-72829/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" "q-72829/selection/fc4e157478869e2cc16df8ee4cd323015b95523464d3b9a082af315c2a4fb28d" "q-72829/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" "q-72829/selection/35d0af53e25a7911f6d08c6d063fcf9231a1273a16a0f7056530d6f5d5dfbdd8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72829" :question/id #uuid "5d62320a-16d8-5d65-a5c8-38ba023de3aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-72829" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040762/assets/6e2223a7dadd9aeddad0b029bf2ba8fc18bafc74dcaca88346ee2b702029b597.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=-\\sqrt{3}.$  Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $B.$" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies inside $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi $, hence, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ This is the $x$ coordinate of $A.$\n\nTo get another solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +x=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $B$ is  $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72829/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72829"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121127/selection/92d2f15ae09c3ac9a946aa5f0ae081bf1aa0dfb330f836b7b209c9170cb7f2ce" :answer/id #uuid "0c06fb52-4d07-5c4a-bc33-ff6c6dba4942" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={88}^{∘},{268}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121127/selection/31d1a3ae723d01de7c0f290cf69363b02c0f05b66f7bbceec83fdd3445bc2ad8" :answer/id #uuid "29a6a170-f56e-557a-9f9a-5c603988a9aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={70}^{∘},{250}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121127/selection/382e3623a28a47458cc3498a0f8141567ada7ba27d803e43b796d666b2d9275a" :answer/id #uuid "6e6568cd-5b34-5130-b80e-b2a441700382" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={63}^{∘},{243}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121127/selection/14f2fc9a4777ac2c729af8198a11233573771db49c295eab49d8eec27911b297" :answer/id #uuid "cf942574-5afe-520f-af8a-2653cf6ba03e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={76}^{∘},{256}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121127/selection/4fa9cd09c18075da603cbd6274091b86695a9beb7e85266552378338dec6ab62" :answer/id #uuid "89ec9b3c-2799-501a-b918-197d33421d44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={83}^{∘},{263}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121127/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fabc99b9-5ea2-5ad4-8bd5-e2dd7f0f7d48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121127/selection/4fa9cd09c18075da603cbd6274091b86695a9beb7e85266552378338dec6ab62" :answer-field/choices ["q-121127/selection/92d2f15ae09c3ac9a946aa5f0ae081bf1aa0dfb330f836b7b209c9170cb7f2ce" "q-121127/selection/31d1a3ae723d01de7c0f290cf69363b02c0f05b66f7bbceec83fdd3445bc2ad8" "q-121127/selection/382e3623a28a47458cc3498a0f8141567ada7ba27d803e43b796d666b2d9275a" "q-121127/selection/14f2fc9a4777ac2c729af8198a11233573771db49c295eab49d8eec27911b297" "q-121127/selection/4fa9cd09c18075da603cbd6274091b86695a9beb7e85266552378338dec6ab62"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121127" :question/id #uuid "9cd45f06-c66b-580b-8617-33b2a6b66d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-121127" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=8$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ rounded to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(8)=82.874\\,983{…}^{∘}≈{82.87}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${82.87}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={82.87}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{82.87}^{∘}={262.87}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx={83}^{∘},{263}^{∘}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-121127/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121127"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321873/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "73e909f5-78ee-53fe-bb18-bede70ec9494" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321873/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "445054b9-825a-5ce0-b82b-ff86e3dd2d9d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321873/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-321873/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321873/field-2/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18" :answer/id #uuid "9070e76c-7a27-5852-9983-b8430eef8d6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "180" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321873/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c07805b2-10ab-579e-b77b-512c5b8c8ed1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321873/field-2/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18" :answer-field/choices ["q-321873/field-2/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321873" :question/id #uuid "9a84cfd7-c56d-5efb-9a8c-2be7100fb694" :question/math-academy-id "q-321873" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=0$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)={0}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${0}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={0}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{x}_{1}={180}^{∘}+{0}^{∘}={180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=180\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321873/field-1" "q-321873/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321873"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
